Software Requirements

1. Functional Requirements

Customer

- Customer can register and login.
- Customer can manage personal profile details.
- Customer can add and manage home appliances.
- Customer can create a maintenance/service request.
- Customer can view service request status.
- Customer can view previous service history.

Technician

- Technician can login into the system.
- Technician can view assigned service requests.
- Technician can view customer and appliance details.
- Technician can update service status.
- Technician can add service remarks.

Admin

- Admin can login into the system.
- Admin can manage customers and technicians.
- Admin can manage appliance categories.
- Admin can view and manage service requests.
- Admin can assign technicians to service requests.
- Admin can monitor completed and pending services.

2. Non-Functional Requirements

Performance

- The system should respond quickly to user requests.
- The application should support multiple users.

Security

- User login details should be protected.
- Only authorized users can access their features.

Usability

- The system should have a simple and user-friendly interface.
- Users should easily navigate through the application.

Reliability

- Service data should be stored safely.
- The system should maintain accurate service records.

Maintainability

- The application should have a modular structure.
- Future features should be easy to add.

3. Hardware Requirements

- Computer/Laptop
- Minimum 8GB RAM
- Internet connection

4. Software Requirements

- Java
- Spring Boot
- MySQL
- HTML, CSS, JavaScript
- Maven
- Git and GitHub
- VS Code / IntelliJ IDEA
